/**
 * A local TCP port that maps onto a port inside a machine.
 *
 * A real resource, unlike {@link Machine}: it holds a bound socket and a
 * running accept loop, so it has something to release and
 * {@link PortForward.close} releases it. Use `async with` / `await using`,
 * or hold it for as long as the port should exist -- letting it be
 * collected also stops the forward.
 *
 * Connections are tunnelled per accepted socket, so several clients may
 * share one forward.
 */
